{% doc %}
  The promotional pill, account control and cart control.

  ## The cart count is Liquid, never JavaScript

  `sections/cart-drawer.liquid` names this section in its `data-sections`, so
  every cart mutation re-renders the header through the Section Rendering API
  and the number arrives already correct. Counting items in the browser as well
  gives two sources of truth that disagree the moment a discount removes a line,
  and the one the customer sees is the wrong one.

  ## Why the account control is sometimes a disclosure

  With no account menu set it is a plain link to the login or account page —
  one target, one destination, nothing to expand. With a menu set it becomes a
  `<details>` handled by the same `<nav-menu>` code as the main navigation, so
  the animation, the hover intent and the Escape handling are not written twice.

  Parameters:
    cart_is_drawer     (boolean, required)
    cart_count_display (string, required)  Already padded if the merchant asked

  @example
    {% render 'header-actions', cart_is_drawer: true, cart_count_display: '02' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign st = section.settings
  assign show_labels = false
  if st.utility_style == 'text'
    assign show_labels = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="site-header__actions"{% unless st.promo_show_mobile %} data-promo-desktop-only{% endunless %}>
  {%- comment -%}
    One text, not two. The inner pill is the design and it stays exactly as it
    was; what changed is where its words come from.

    There used to be a Label setting *and* a Badge setting: the label sat outside
    the inner pill, in the outer pill's own colour, and was hidden by CSS below
    1400px - so on most screens a merchant typing into Label saw nothing happen.
    Badge did all the visible work. Label now feeds the pill, and Badge is gone.

    Still a link only when it points somewhere, and a static pill when it does
    not, rather than an anchor with `href="#"` that sends the customer back to
    the top of the page.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if st.promo_label != blank -%}
    {%- if st.promo_link != blank -%}
      <a class="site-header__promo" href="{{ st.promo_link }}">
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="site-header__promo">
    {%- endif -%}
      {% render 'icon', icon: 'tag', size: 14, class: 'site-header__promo-icon' %}
      <span class="site-header__promo-badge">{{ st.promo_label | escape }}</span>
    {%- if st.promo_link != blank -%}</a>{%- else -%}</span>{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Search sits with the other controls, immediately before the account button.

    It used to be slotted independently, which meant it could land on the far
    side of the navigation from the cart — three icon controls in two clusters
    with the menu between them. Customers reach for search, account and cart as
    one group; splitting them costs a scan of the whole row.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if st.show_search -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="site-header__action site-header__action--search"
      data-overlay-open="SearchDrawer"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-controls="SearchDrawer"
      aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.open_search' | t }}"
    >
      {% render 'icon', icon: 'search', size: 20 %}
      {%- if show_labels -%}
        <span class="site-header__action-label">{{ 'general.search.title' | t }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </button>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if st.show_account -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign account_url = routes.account_login_url
      if customer
        assign account_url = routes.account_url
      endif
    -%}

    {%- if st.account_menu != blank and st.account_menu.links.size > 0 -%}
      <nav-disclosure class="site-header__account">
      <details class="nav__details" data-nav-details data-kind="sub">
        <summary
          class="site-header__action site-header__action--account"
          data-nav-summary
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-label="{{ 'sections.header.account' | t }}"
        >
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'account', size: 18 %}
          {%- if show_labels -%}
            <span class="site-header__action-label">{{ 'sections.header.account' | t }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </summary>

        <div class="nav__panel nav__panel--sub nav__panel--end" data-nav-panel>
          <div class="nav__panel-inner">
            <ul class="dropdown dropdown--sub" role="list">
              {%- for link in st.account_menu.links -%}
                <li class="dropdown__item">
                  <a class="dropdown__link" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
      </nav-disclosure>
    {%- else -%}
      <a
        class="site-header__action site-header__action--account"
        href="{{ account_url }}"
        aria-label="{{ 'sections.header.account' | t }}"
      >
        {% render 'icon', icon: 'account', size: 18 %}
        {%- if show_labels -%}
          <span class="site-header__action-label">{{ 'sections.header.account' | t }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <a
    class="site-header__action site-header__action--cart"
    href="{{ routes.cart_url }}"
    {% if cart_is_drawer %}
      data-overlay-open="CartDrawer"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-controls="CartDrawer"
    {% endif %}
    aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.open_cart' | t }}"
  >
    {% render 'icon', icon: 'cart', size: 18 %}
    <span class="site-header__cart-count" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart_count_display }}</span>
    <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'sections.header.cart_count' | t: count: cart.item_count }}</span>
  </a>
</div>
